//! The `ruby-align` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property defines the
//! distribution of the different ruby elements over the base.
//!
//! Initial: space-around. Inherited: yes.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - center: Is a keyword indicating that the ruby will be aligned at the middle of the base text.
//! - space-around: Is a keyword indicating that the extra space will be distributed between the
//! elements of the ruby, and around it.
//! - space-between: Is a keyword indicating that the extra space will be distributed between the
//! elements of the ruby.
//! - start: Is a keyword indicating that the ruby will be aligned with the start of the base text.
//!
//! Grammar: start | center | space-between | space-around
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-ruby-1/#propdef-ruby-align
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/ruby-align
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Additional value descriptions: Microsoft (MIT).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

